From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin <robinei@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 16:13:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/dsi: Apply the 320 MHz minimum cdclk for DSI on CHV
 too

EXPERIMENT, not for upstream until tested.

Commit c8dae55a8ced ("drm/i915/vlv: Add cdclk workaround for DSI") made
DSI on Valleyview require a cdclk of at least 320000 kHz, because at
266667 kHz a Chuwi Vi8 panel showed the image shifted with wraparound
and sometimes wrong colors, the panel sampling the stream from mid-line.
Cherryview has the same DSI block, but vlv_dsi_min_cdclk() returns 0
for it.

On a GPD Win 1 (Cherry Trail, 720x1280 DSI, 61.1 MHz pixel clock) the
driver runs cdclk at 266667 kHz, and under load the picture
intermittently ends up split (bottom part on top), sometimes with red
and blue swapped, until the next modeset; MIPI_INTR_STAT then has
DPI_FIFO_UNDERRUN latched while the pipe reports no FIFO underrun.

Extend the minimum to Cherryview. 320000 kHz is the maximum cdclk there
(intel_update_max_cdclk()), so it is always reachable.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
index 877eab7..781af8e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
@@ -1761,10 +1761,10 @@ int vlv_dsi_min_cdclk(const struct intel_crtc_state *crtc_state)
 		return 0;
 
 	/*
-	 * On Valleyview some DSI panels lose (v|h)sync when the clock is lower
-	 * than 320000KHz.
+	 * On Valleyview and Cherryview some DSI panels lose (v|h)sync when the
+	 * clock is lower than 320000KHz.
 	 */
-	if (display->platform.valleyview)
+	if (display->platform.valleyview || display->platform.cherryview)
 		return 320000;
 
 	/*
